; Element-failure-analysis demo lattice (HELIX)
;
; A compact PIP-II-like superconducting section: four RF cavities focused
; by three solenoids.  Enough cavities that a single cavity failure can be
; compensated by its neighbours (the MYRRHA/LightWin local-compensation
; scheme), and a mix of element types (cavity + solenoid) so the failure
; sweep ranks both.
;
; Beam seed (set via the run script / the Failures tab beam config):
;   proton, 2.5 MeV, ~0 mA (envelope; raise for MP loss studies), 162.5 MHz
;
; No ADJUST/SET cards are needed — the failure study injects failures, and
; the compensation step injects its own ADJUST/SET cards on the chosen
; compensation zone.
;
TITLE Failure-analysis demo
FREQ 162.5

DRIFT 50 20.0
SOLENOID 100 0.30 20.0
DRIFT 40 20.0
GAP 800000 -25.0 20.0 0          ; cavity 1 (0.80 MV)

DRIFT 40 20.0
SOLENOID 100 0.30 20.0
DRIFT 40 20.0
GAP 1000000 -22.0 20.0 0         ; cavity 2 (1.00 MV)

DRIFT 40 20.0
SOLENOID 100 0.32 20.0
DRIFT 40 20.0
GAP 1000000 -20.0 20.0 0         ; cavity 3 (1.00 MV)

DRIFT 40 20.0
GAP 1200000 -20.0 20.0 0         ; cavity 4 (1.20 MV)
DRIFT 50 20.0

END
